abstract:
Stable light rings, which are associated with spacetime instabilities, are known to exist in four-dimensional stationary axisymmetric spacetimes that solve the Einstein-Maxwell equations (so-called electrovacuum solutions, with Faraday tensor $F_{μν} 
eq 0$); however, they are not permitted in pure vacuum ($F_{μν} = 0$). In this work, we extend this result to spacetimes with a non-zero cosmological constant $Λ$. In particular, we demonstrate that stable light rings are permitted in $Λ$-electrovacuum ($F_{μν} 
eq 0$, $Λ
eq 0$), but ruled out in $Λ$-vacuum ($F_{μν} = 0$, $Λ
eq 0$).
